          "end": 1002
        },
        {
          "text": "Vihaan Kumar Vs. State of Haryana and Another, 2025 SCC OnLine SC 269",
          "label": "PRECEDENT",
          "start": 1018,
          "end": 1087
        }
      ],
      "in_summary": true,
      "summary_section": "arguments",
      "summary_sent_score": 0.28494128584861755
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 8,
      "text": "Learned State Counsel admits that the grounds of arrest, in writing, were not communicated to the applicant.",
      "rhetorical_role": "ARG_PETITIONER",
      "start": 1092,
      "end": 1200,
      "entities": [],
      "in_summary": true,
      "summary_section": "arguments",
      "summary_sent_score": 0.1295420527458191
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 9,
      "text": "6. In para 21 of the judgment in the case of Vihaan Kumar (supra), the Hon'ble Supreme Court observed as follows:-\n\"21.",
      "rhetorical_role": "NONE",
      "start": 1201,
      "end": 1321,
      "entities": [
        {
          "text": "Vihaan Kumar",
          "label": "PRECEDENT",
          "start": 1247,
          "end": 1259
        },
        {
          "text": "Supreme Court",
          "label": "COURT",
          "start": 1281,
          "end": 1294
        }
      ],
      "in_summary": false
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 10,
      "text": "Therefore, we conclude:\na) The requirement of informing a person arrested of grounds of arrest is a mandatory requirement of Article 22(1);\n. . .",
      "rhetorical_role": "NONE",
      "start": 1322,
      "end": 1467,
      "entities": [
        {
          "text": "Article 22(1)",
          "label": "PROVISION",
